.TH YOGA-WINDOWS-VM 1 "November 2026" "lenovo-yoga-c940-14iil-windows-vm" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yoga-windows-vm \- run the Windows install of a Lenovo Yoga C940 in a KVM virtual machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yoga-windows-vm
.I command
.RI [ argument ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manages a libvirt/QEMU virtual machine that boots the Windows installation already on the laptop's NVMe drive.
The default mode is an overlay: the real Windows partition is never written.
Commands that change system state re-run themselves with sudo unless run as root.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Build the virtual GPT/ESP disk, the MSDM copy and the overlay, and define the VM (root).
.TP
.B start " [--viewer]"
Start the VM, headless unless --viewer is given.
.TP
.B view
Open virt-viewer on the running VM.
.TP
.B launch
Start the VM if needed and open the viewer (used by the GNOME launcher).
.TP
.B stop
ACPI shutdown; wait SHUTDOWN_WAIT seconds; destroy the VM only as a last resort.
.TP
.B status
Show the disk mode, the VM state, the host mount state and whether autostart is on.
.TP
.BR mode " overlay|raw"
Switch the disk mode. Raw mode needs --enable-raw-writes and the VM must be off.
.TP
.BR autostart " on|off"
Start the VM at host boot and stop it cleanly at host shutdown (default off).
.TP
.B remount
Remount the Windows partition on the host if the VM is off (root).
.TP
.B reset-overlay
Discard the overlay, that is, the Windows changes made in overlay mode (root).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/yoga-windows-vm/yoga-windows-vm.conf
Settings (disk, domain name, data directory, shutdown wait).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR virsh (1),
.BR virt-viewer (1)
